    description: "Regression found by the 2026-11-02 awaits_bakeoff_validation drain (record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_queue_11022026/VERDICTS.md). WI-vidof's corpus claim (gatling: 15 false scala.io.StdIn ipc_recv chains -> 0) reads no_move on dev b20da19ff3: all 15 are back, every one a LogFileReader.scala subclass call (FirstPassParser / SecondPassParser) to the superclass's own readInt / readLong / readBoolean / readByte.\n\nBISECTED (git bisect run over 618 commits, probe = gatling StdIn chain count): first bad commit 74ffde9e1f \"fix(scala): a call on a project object or companion resolves where Scala binds the name (WI-kipol)\". Its inherited_calls change indexes `object` kinds into class_ids_by_name.\n\nMECHANISM: gatling declares `private object LogFileParser` ABOVE `private abstract class LogFileParser[T]` in the same file. type_hierarchy._resolve_method_class_id credits a method to its owner by NAME plus \"first same-file namesake\", so LogFileParser.readInt went to the object. The walk FirstPassParser -> (class) LogFileParser found no readInt, the stub kept no superseded_by, and the stub took the StdIn row by short name. Minimal fixture (companion object first) reproduces it; dropping the object makes it resolve. Not caused by PR #2004 (the pre-#2004 tree 64a87d13ff shows the same 15).\n\nFIX SHAPE: the owner is the same-file candidate whose span CONTAINS the method (INV-mozas: position, never name), tightest first; the old same-file pick stays only when no candidate contains it."  # 9b1b
    fields: {}  # 9b1b
