  nonce: 893b  # 893b
  message: "Fixed in PR #2012 (dev d9d6f46b5d + dfe0abf947). Root cause: type_hierarchy._resolve_method_class_id credited a method to the FIRST same-file namesake, so a Scala companion object declared above its class took the class’s methods once WI-kipol indexed object kinds. Fix: the owner is the same-file candidate whose span encloses the method, tightest first (INV-mozas, position never name); the old same-file pick stays only when none encloses it. Span.encloses is now the one containment test (router_routes / controller_routes dropped their private copies). BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE, the filed repro re-run: hypergumbo survey + io-boundaries --format json on whole_bunch_of_repos/gatling with the merged code (tree 6a44b2b2af, code-identical to dfe0abf947 by git diff over packages/docs/.ci): scala.io.StdIn chains 15 -> 0 (lab bakeoff_queue_11022026/io/gatling.merged.json). Production-path test: test_short_name_bound_call.py::test_io_boundaries_keeps_the_stdin_read_and_drops_the_inherited_call[companion_first] (red on the old owner pick: owner followed declaration order, shown in the drain record) plus unit tests in test_type_hierarchy_linker.py (both declaration orders). Corpus A/B (lab bakeoff_queue_11022026/fix_ab/): gatling 63 call sites newly resolved, 17 retargeted, 2 lost; sbt 40 retargeted to the class over its companion, 9 lost, ~356 false sibling-to-sibling dispatches_to removed; okhttp and sherpa-onnx unchanged. The 11 lost sites were companion-object members reached only through the misassignment; residual WI-damuj-tujad-nuvot-funim-fodug-sidok-tidot-pulon carries their real route (import binding)."  # 893b
